        <p style="margin: 0 0 1rem; font-size: 1.0625rem; line-height: 1.8; color: var(--text);">Yes. Insulated plasterboard adds thermal insulation to external walls. For the uninsulated solid 9-inch brick walls typical of Maidstone's Victorian terraces (Maidstone central, Bearsted and Loose), a 50-80mm insulated plasterboard (PIR or phenolic) can reduce U-values from around 2.1 W/m²K to 0.30 W/m²K, meeting current Part L retrofit targets.</p>
<p style="margin: 0 0 1rem; font-size: 1.0625rem; line-height: 1.8; color: var(--text);">Three common insulation options for Maidstone properties:</p>
<p style="margin: 0 0 1rem; font-size: 1.0625rem; line-height: 1.8; color: var(--text);">- PIR (polyisocyanurate): best thermal performance per mm, ~0.022 W/mK, thinnest build-up
